/-!
# Lifting invariant elements across an invariant nilpotent ideal

Let `B'` be a ring with two ring maps `s, t : B' → C'`, let `J ⊆ B'` be a nilpotent ideal
which is *invariant*, in the sense that its two extensions `s(J)C'` and `t(J)C'` agree, and
write `B = B'/J`, `C = C'/JC'`. Suppose the reduction is the Čech nerve of a faithfully flat
ring map `A → B`: the two induced maps `B ⇉ C` exhibit `C` as generated by their images, and
the triple level `D'`, with three maps `C' ⇉ D'` satisfying the cosimplicial identities, reduces
to a ring `D` mapping to `B ⊗[A] C`. If moreover one of the maps `C' → D'` is flat, then every
element of `A`, read in `B`, lifts to an element `b'` of `B'` with `s b' = t b'`.

Geometrically: `B' = Γ(U')` for an affine étale chart `U'` of an algebraic space `X'`,
`C' = Γ(U' ×_{X'} U')`, `D' = Γ(U' ×_{X'} U' ×_{X'} U')`, `J` cuts out the chart
`U = Spec B` of a thickening `X ⊂ X'` of finite order, and `X = Spec A` is affine; the
conclusion is that the restriction `Γ(X', 𝒪) → Γ(X, 𝒪)` is surjective, the input of the proof
for finite order thickenings of Stacks 05ZQ and 05ZR.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Descent.C1573.AdicGradedPiece`: the graded piece `I^k / I^{k+1}` of the `I`-adic
  filtration.
* `Stacks.Descent.C1573.AdicGradedPiece.map`: its functoriality along a ring map.
* `Stacks.Descent.C1573.EqualizerLiftData`: the rings and maps of the situation above.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Descent.C1573.exact_of_lTensor_contraction`: exactness of a two-step complex of
  modules over a ring `A` is reflected from a contraction of its base change along a faithfully
  flat `A → B`, read through a surjective comparison in degree zero and an injective one in
  degree one.
* `Stacks.Descent.C1573.EqualizerLiftData.exact_gradedDiff`: the obstruction complex
  `J^k/J^{k+1} → JC'^k/JC'^{k+1} → JD'^k/JD'^{k+1}` is exact in the middle.
* `Stacks.Descent.C1573.EqualizerLiftData.exists_eq_of_isNilpotent`: the lifting statement.

## Implementation notes

The obstruction to lifting an invariant element across `J^k/J^{k+1}` is a `1`-cocycle of the
graded piece `gr^k` of the `J`-adic filtration of the cosimplicial ring `B' ⇉ C' ⇛ D'`, and the
point is that it is a coboundary. That graded piece is a module over the Čech nerve
`B ⇉ B ⊗[A] B ⇛ …` of the faithfully flat map `A → B`, cartesian over the coface into the last
factor because `C' → D'` is flat. Rather than descending it to an `A`-module (Stacks 023N) and
then applying exactness of the Amitsur complex (Stacks 023M), we base change the obstruction
complex along `A → B` once more: the new factor of `B` sits in the last slot, multiplying it into
the last slot of `C` is a contracting homotopy, and faithful flatness reflects exactness. All
that is needed of the cartesian property is the *injectivity* of the comparison
`B ⊗[A] gr^k(C') → gr^k(D')`, which is proved by writing down a left inverse through the
flatness of `C' → D'`, and the *surjectivity* of `B ⊗[A] gr^k(B') → gr^k(C')`, which needs no
flatness at all.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 023M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/023M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05ZQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05ZR)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

